KG42.register("rules-393b7cf3d69fb3c02cde1046",{"id":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R016","paper":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R016","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Consumers with flexible demand are included as players in the modeled P2P bidding game. Scope: The modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game. Condition: The consumer has flexible demand. Consumer participants are not aggregated with other consumers or prosumers to achieve higher benefits through cooperation. Scope: Competitive-participation assumption of the Elecbay P2P bidding simulation.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Competitive-participation assumption of the Elecbay P2P bidding simulation. | The modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-30","v141-b-g01-ev-36"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-TH001","symbol":"n","meaning":"number of players in the modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-36"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-TH002","symbol":"N","meaning":"set of players in the modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"N = {1, 2, …, i, …, n}"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-36"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Consumers with flexible demand are included as players in the modeled P2P bidding game. Scope: The modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game. Condition: The consumer has flexible demand.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-36"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Consumer participants are not aggregated with other consumers or prosumers to achieve higher benefits through cooperation. Scope: Competitive-participation assumption of the Elecbay P2P bidding simulation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-30"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The player set of the modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game is denoted N = {1, 2, …, i, …, n}, where n is the number of players in the game and N is the set of players. The source states that the players are energy consumers and prosumers with flexible demand. Scope: The modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game. Condition: The player has flexible demand. This rule's frozen graph declares only participation.consumer, so this constraint records the player-set formula as it bears on consumer participation; the prosumer subset is not asserted by this rule.","expression":"N = {1, 2, \\ldots, i, \\ldots, n}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-TH001","v141-c-R016-TH002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-36"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-30","location":{"location_id":"src-c1934be9b4-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M03-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"4. Simulation of P2P bidding","anchor_text":"means energy consumers and prosumers are not aggregated with is each other for achieving higher bene","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"1. The P2P energy trading through “Elecbay” is competitive, which means energy consumers and prosumers are not aggregated with each other for achieving higher benefits via co-operation. 2. Energy consumers and prosumers are considered as “good citizens”, who contribute to maintaining local energy balance. 3. Energy suppliers (i.e. the electricity retailers) are passive peers in this paper. They buy energy from energy prosumers with low unit prices, and sell energy to energy consumers and prosumers with high unit prices. Energy consumers and prosumers consider energy suppliers as the last peer to trade with during the P2P bidding. This assumption is consistent with the reality in many countries such as the UK. 4. Service charges of Elecbay are neglected in this paper"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-36","location":{"location_id":"src-c1934be9b4-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"4.2.1. The formulation of P2P bidding as a non-cooperative game","anchor_text":"ed the equilibrium strategies of the other players, and no player has any es thing to gain by changi","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"4.2.1. The formulation of P2P bidding as a non-cooperative game. Players of the game are energy consumers and prosumers with flexible demand. Denote N = {1, 2, …, i …, n}, where n is the number of players in the game, and N is the set of players in the game."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No design or operational decision variable is declared for consumer participation. The source's flexible-demand ON/OFF strategy s_i^{j_i} and its selection are part of the bidding/strategy formulation (candidate evidence v141-b-g01-ev-37, v141-b-g02-E06) and are not represented by this rule's frozen V=[\"participation.consumer\"].","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-bidding","v141-a-M03-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-36","quote":"Players of the game are energy consumers and prosumers with flexible demand."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-30","quote":"The P2P energy trading through “Elecbay” is competitive, which means energy consumers and prosumers are not aggregated with each other for achieving higher benefits via co-operation."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"71489a9d12d57e73782faeaf56427fcafa2d1848464efcefb3410f910972f7d6","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Applicability=formalized because C003 faithfully transcribes the player-set formula from the rule's candidate evidence v141-b-g01-ev-36. C001 and C002 remain procedural not_formalized because they state inclusion and non-aggregation assumptions rather than equations. No design/operational x is declared for consumer participation; theta carries the source-defined player count n and player set N that determine the set of players to which participation.consumer belongs. B evidence is unreviewed candidate support; this patch does not claim independent source audit or verified source correctness.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-TH001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"n is the cardinality of the player set N in the source's P2P bidding game; consumer participants are members of N, so the parameter is bound to the consumer-participation node. No edge is asserted because the frozen rule has E=[]."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-TH002","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"N is the source-defined set of players in the modeled non-cooperative P2P bidding game; the consumer-participation node represents consumers with flexible demand being among the members of N. No edge is asserted because the frozen rule has E=[]."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C003","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The player-set definition N = {1, 2, …, i, …, n} from the same source section establishes the set of game players to which consumer participation belongs; it is attached to the consumer-participation node because the rule's V contains only participation.consumer. The prosumer part is handled by the separate prosumer rule and is not moved here. No edge is asserted because E=[]."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
